Chapter 6: Verification–Recovery Tradeoff

6.1 Budget Allocation

Total budget B split as B_R+B_V=B:

R(B_R)=1-e^{-\alpha B_R},\qquad V(B_V)=1-e^{-\beta B_V},\qquad F=0.

s(u)=1-(1-G)e^{-\alpha u}-Ge^{-\beta B}e^{(\beta-\alpha)u},\qquad u=B_R.

6.2 Three-Regime Allocation Theorem

Theorem 6.1 (Global structure of the optimal allocation). Let \alpha,\beta>0, G\in(0,1), u\in[0,B]. Then:

(a) Strict concavity. s''(u)=-(1-G)\alpha^2e^{-\alpha u}-G(\beta-\alpha)^2e^{-\beta B}e^{(\beta-\alpha)u}<0. Consequently, the constrained maximizer exists and is unique.

(b) Regime classification. The unique maximizer u^\ast satisfies exactly one of:

· (I) Policy-dominated: \beta\le\alpha or G\le\alpha/\beta. Then u^\ast=B.
· (II) Interior: \beta>\alpha and \frac{\alpha}{\beta}<G<\frac{\alpha e^{\beta B}}{\beta-\alpha+\alpha e^{\beta B}}. Then
  u^\ast=B-\frac{1}{\beta}\ln\!\left(\frac{G(\beta-\alpha)}{(1-G)\alpha}\right),\qquad 0<u^\ast<B.
· (III) Verification-dominated: \beta>\alpha and G\ge\frac{\alpha e^{\beta B}}{\beta-\alpha+\alpha e^{\beta B}}. Then u^\ast=0.

Proof.

(a) Immediate from s''<0.

(b) First-order condition:

\frac{ds}{du}=(1-G)\alpha e^{-\alpha u}+G(\alpha-\beta)e^{-\alpha u-\beta(B-u)}=0.

Solving gives the interior critical point

u^\ast=B-\frac{1}{\beta}\ln\!\left(\frac{G(\beta-\alpha)}{(1-G)\alpha}\right).

This is interior iff 0<u^\ast<B, equivalent to \frac{\alpha}{\beta}<G<\frac{\alpha e^{\beta B}}{\beta-\alpha+\alpha e^{\beta B}}. Boundary cases follow from strict concavity. \square

Corollary 6.1 (Three-phase allocation).

\boxed{\text{Policy-dominated}\to\text{Mixed}\to\text{Verification-dominated}.}

6.3 Comparative Statics

Proposition 6.1. Under Regime II:

\frac{\partial u^\ast}{\partial B}=1,\qquad \frac{\partial u^\ast}{\partial\alpha}>0,\qquad \frac{\partial u^\ast}{\partial G}<0.

Proof. Direct differentiation of the closed form. The second term in u^\ast is independent of B, so \partial u^\ast/\partial B=1. \square

Remark 6.1. Version 3.0 incorrectly stated that u^\ast is decreasing in B with a log-correction. The derivative is exactly 1 in the interior regime.

