Chapter 7: State-Dependent Recovery

7.1 Recovery as Kernel Modification

Definition 7.1 (Recovery-modified kernel).

P_\rho(s_{t+1}\mid s_t,a_t,\text{failure})=\int_\Pi P_\pi(s_{t+1}\mid s_t,a_t)\,d\rho(\pi).

Definition 7.2 (Long-horizon reachability). Let G\subseteq\mathcal X be a goal set in state space. Then

R_{\text{long}}^{\text{SD}}(\Pi,\rho)=P\!\left[\exists t\le T:s_t\in G\right]

under the recovery-modified kernel.

Remark 7.1. Version 3.0 defined R_{\text{long}}^{\text{SD}}=P[\exists t:\Phi(\tau_{0:t})\in\mathcal G], which requires \Phi to be defined on partial trajectories. Definition 7.2 uses state-space reachability, which is standard and well-defined.

7.2 Basin-of-Attraction Dominance

Definition 7.3 (Basin of attraction). \mathcal A(G) is the set of states from which G is reachable with positive probability under P_\rho.

Definition 7.4 (Basin dominance). P_\rho is basin-dominant over P if \pi_\rho(\mathcal A(G))\ge\pi(\mathcal A(G)).

Conjecture 7.1 (State-dependent recovery dominance). If P_\rho is basin-dominant over P, then a policy with lower R_{\text{init}} but higher G_R can achieve higher long-horizon reachability.

Remark 7.2. This is stated as a conjecture. Its proof requires ergodic-theoretic arguments relating recovery-kernel ergodicity to long-horizon reachability.

