Chapter 11: Theorem Hierarchy

Theorem A — Classical embedding. \Omega(x)=\{f(x)\} recovers deterministic correctness.

Theorem B — Feasible-set monotonicity. R_2>R_1\Rightarrow B^\ast(R_2)\le B^\ast(R_1).

Theorem C — Shadow-price characterization. -dB^\ast/dR=\lambda^\ast where regularity holds.

Theorem D — Verification–Recovery allocation. Three-regime strict-concavity theorem.

Theorem E — Recovery feasible-set expansion. G_2>G_1\Rightarrow B^\ast_{G_2}(R)\ge B^\ast_{G_1}(R).

Conjecture F — Recovery curvature. Recovery reduces the marginal cost of reliability.

